# Generated by scripts/build_assets.py, deliberately not committed.
#
# The root .gitattributes says of these formats: "If the pipeline later imports
# .fbx / .glb source meshes, add them here BEFORE the first commit, not after."
# That needs Git LFS, and git-lfs is not installed in the container this kit was
# built in -- pushing this repository's first LFS objects from here could leave
# pointer files with no objects behind them. That is the founder's call, not a
# side effect of an asset session.
#
# Nothing is lost. validate_assets.py proves the build is deterministic (every
# module rebuilt in a clean scene hashes identically, and the hashes are in
# validation/VALIDATION_REPORT.json), so
#
#     python3 scripts/build_assets.py
#
# reproduces byte-identical meshes in about three minutes. README.md has the
# exact order to follow if the meshes should be committed under LFS instead.
exports/
source/

# Blender's own leavings
*.blend1
*.blend2
__pycache__/
